# The live install: the SQLite database, its WAL sidecars, the nightly backups
# and every uploaded receipt. Excluded for two reasons — a developer's real team
# finances must never be baked into a published image, and /app/data is a mount
# point in the container, so anything copied here would just be shadowed anyway.
data/

# Legacy Postgres bind mount, from before the single-container port. Still
# ignored because it is owned by the postgres user and unreadable to the build,
# which fails the whole build with a permission error rather than skipping it.
db/data

# Screenshots and long-form docs. Only the README-facing material, and it is
# several megabytes of PNG that the build has no use for.
docs/

# Never let secrets into an image that might get pushed somewhere.
.env
.env.*
secrets/

# Rebuilt inside the image; copying them in would shadow the build output and
# risks baking in a host-arch node_modules.
node_modules
*/node_modules
server/dist
web/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
*.log
backups/
README.md
LICENSE
